message.content:
This is a women's knit sweater of 81% polyamide (synthetic fiber) and 19% metallic fiber, so it falls in heading 6110 (jerseys, pullovers, cardigans, etc., knitted). Subheading 6110.30 covers man-made fibers. The fiber content is predominantly man-made, with metallic yarn treated as a textile material, so 6110.30 applies.

Within 6110.30, the women's or girls' sweaters and pullovers fall under 6110.30.30 (other, women's), with the statistical suffix 6110.30.3053 for women's or girls' sweaters, other. Subheading 6110.30.20 is for containing 23% or more by weight of leather, and 6110.30.30 is "Other: Sweaters, pullovers, sweatshirts..." in the men's/boys' or women's/girls' breakdown. The women's sweaters statistical code is 6110.30.3059 (women's or girls' other) or 6110.30.3053 (sweaters). Of these, 6110.30.3053 is "Sweaters: Women's or girls'", so that is the one I choose.

{"hts_code": "6110.30.3053", "reason": "Women's knit sweater of man-made fibers (81% polyamide, 19% metallic) is classified in heading 6110, subheading 6110.30 as a women's sweater of man-made fibers."}
